  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Lucky prepared his armies to defend Mato Grosso and the 
surrounding provinces.
  Quintilian returned to Valhalla, having done his best to execute his 
duties.


  Thus endeth the adventures of Lucky for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Brunhilda (#86) has arrived in the Atl. Ocean 1908 from Mali.
  Ewaine (#149) hiked into Amazonia.  He had grown bored with Venezuela and 
was attracted there by rumors of its wonderful scotch and even more 
wonderful champagnes.


  Here is the financial report for Lucky's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Lucky was left with 11 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Hecate
To: Lucky

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I prepared my forces to defend the Atl. Ocean 2008 and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Hecate


From: Quintilian
To: Lucky

  Honored Sovereign, 

  I returned to Valhalla, having done my best to execute my duties.


  Thy humble servant,   Quintilian


